        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'v0.15.2: Bash-compatibility fixes. On Windows a lowercase spelling of a reserved name (path, tmp, temp, home, os) is its own variable, as in bash; Windows spellings (windir, SystemRoot) list upper-cased as in Git Bash, and set -x prints the bash name. unset -n drops a nameref, unset reads clustered options (-vn, -nf) and --, a nameref or attribute declared in a subshell ends with it, and a nameref declared with no target is listed, takes its target from the first write (assignment, for, read, printf -v), is unbound under set -u, and becomes an array when one is assigned to it. fc -l ranges, fc -s and fc -e - re-run as bash 5.2 does, in the caller (return, break, local), and history takes -d ranges, -p expansion and -anrw; history modifiers chain (:s, :gs, :&). A quoted builtin name (local, export, eval, return) runs the builtin and skips any alias, and a quoted declaration builtin splits its words as bash does. A return inside a redirected group, loop, if or case leaves the function; a run-time local is always local. Bash text built at run time (eval, trap, a nested bash -c) never runs as PowerShell. Under set -e a redirect that cannot open its file ends the shell. bash FILE exits 127 when FILE is missing and 126 when it is a directory. Array writes in a pipe stage or command substitution are several times faster. Container setups for Windows (Nano Server, Server Core) and Linux in docker/, with a CI smoke test. sed, grep, expr and find share one GNU regex translator (sed: last-regex reuse, N line numbers, -f error lines, s/y escapes). $SECONDS counts from the shell start and honours assignment; && / || operands record PIPESTATUS. Hosts: on Linux a session''s warm host no longer exits seconds after each command; nested and overflow commands run on warm slots, not fresh hosts; install drains old hosts once idle instead of killing a running command (host drain). v0.15.1: Bash-compatibility fixes. A pipe stage is a subshell: cd, source, set, umask and the other state builtins in it change nothing in the caller. Refused assignments (readonly, a[]=, circular nameref) drop the rest of the line as bash does, and end the shell under set -e or posix. local -a/-A and declare in a function make a local array; a callee''s array write reaches the caller''s local; a local''s attributes and nameref are its frame''s. Diagnostics name the script and line (t.sh: line N:) for refusals, bad subscripts, failglob, ambiguous redirects and arithmetic errors; an arithmetic error discards the line. A builtin given too many arguments drops the line; exec reads the stdin it inherits; a piped script (cat f | bash) is read from stdin; env -i no longer clears the host environment; time and timeout pass their pipe byte for byte; every command rejects an option it does not have; on Windows the output of a redirected nohup command run by the Git ls/sh reaches its file, and 2> truncates. v0.15.0: Bash-compatibility release (XFAIL marks in the bash spec suite 140 -> 79). BREAKING: paths a script sees use forward slashes on Windows ($PWD, ~, $HOME, mktemp, realpath print C:/x; input still accepts C:\x and /c/x); bash code no longer resolves PowerShell aliases (gci, iex, r are command not found, 127, unless a function or program has the name; use the full cmdlet name); a nested shell sees exported variables only (x=1; sh -c "echo $x" prints an empty line; use export; a plain prog still sees all). Background jobs: output streams as the job runs, in launch order, with bounded memory; a job reads its own copy of the variables; a job sleep counts from its &. New: kill -SIG $$ and signals sent to a shell pid reach its trap; hash keeps the bash table; BASH_LINENO; --rcfile; a session whose hosts are all busy runs the command on a private host (PSBASH_EXEC_OVERFLOW_MS). Fix: pasted Unicode quote and dash marks no longer break the emitted PowerShell; line tools join a piece without its newline into the next line (printf a | sed); a while-read pipe stage reads lines as they are written; set -e ends a failing pipe stage; exit, break and errexit stop at subshell boundaries; pipefail after && and ||; an assignment sets PIPESTATUS; stopping a child ends its whole process tree; a 2>&1 child keeps its write order; a nested bash streams and is never timed out; a record keeps its trailing empty lines; base64 and od stream endless input; /dev/* names are never opened as files; file redirects write as output is produced; readlink and realpath canonicalize like GNU; kill -l prints the bash signal table; {a,} is one word; command and nohup run #! scripts; command not found carries the bash line prefix. Builtins and variables: help, bind, caller, enable, disown, logout, suspend; PPID, SHLVL, SRANDOM, BASH_SUBSHELL, default IFS; exec N<>file read-write descriptors; a DEBUG trap set on one line fires. Commands: GNU option parsing for uname, shuf, id, ping and tee; seq, tr, touch and install operand errors; date MMDDhhmm; env -C runs pwd in DIR; mkdir dir/; kill -RTMIN+N; a #! script reads the exact bytes piped to it. macOS: scripts no longer die with exit 138 (SIGUSR1 is left to the .NET runtime); stat, signals and ioctl are decoded per OS and arch. Known issues: docs/known-issues.md. v0.14.5: Bash-parity pass: 189 oils spec cases fixed (XFAIL 316 -> 127). Fix: "$@" inside a function reached a command as one joined word (cat "$@" with two files failed) and dash options passed to a function (f -i x) broke grep/head "$@". Fix: a stopped command no longer kills the shared host; a nested ps-bash joins its enclosing session instead of starting a second daemon; ps-bash host list, and host gc removes only orphaned hosts. New: fc, piped bash -i runs as an interactive session, history -a/-w/-r, PROMPT_COMMAND, \D{fmt} in prompts, compgen -X/-A user/-A command, set -v/-n, BASHOPTS, umask -p, mapfile -O, printf %(fmt)T honors TZ, LC_ALL=C counts bytes, kill/wait jobspecs, ulimit soft/hard limits, redirect target globs. Also: GLOBIGNORE, POSIX ERE in =~, octal and invalid arithmetic values, NUL bytes in $( ) and read, printf %q of invalid UTF-8, sed \xHH, cat /dev/zero, a script with a NUL byte is refused as binary, unterminated quotes are syntax errors, failglob and bad substitutions drop the rest of the line, aliases with here-docs, tilde and globstar inside braces. v0.14.4: Resource-leak pass. Fix: a mktemp file a long script still needed was deleted once any shell ran a process substitution five minutes later. Now removed instead of piling up: socket files left by killed hosts, old module extraction directories (about 5 MB per build, kept while any process uses them), and empty mktemp -d directories older than 10 days. A background-job spare host that failed to start is replaced at once. Fix: aliases in plain PowerShell with Import-Module PsBash ("Unable to find type"); $_ in and after a pipeline; exec {fd}>file allocates a descriptor and >&$fd writes to it; bash -i -c sets HISTFILE; a quoted ] does not close a glob bracket. v0.14.3: Bash-compatibility batch (about 140 fixes, checked against bash 5.2). New: chmod (octal and symbolic modes, -R -v -c -f), od, nohup for background processes that outlive the shell, symbolic umask modes, set -a / allexport, $SHELLOPTS, history in scripts; launcher -e, -u, -o and -O apply to the -c string. Fix: unquoted expansions glued to text split as bash splits them, in arguments, $(...), [ ] and extglob patterns; arrays (sparse slices, element initializers in declare/local, subscripts as words, associative key order); namerefs, unset and local scoping; exit and return statuses, errexit, the ERR trap and errtrace; return inside eval text, source searches PATH; exec on stdin/stdout/stderr and numbered descriptors on a simple command; [ ] and [[ ]] operand rules; redirects to /dev/stdout and /dev/stderr; pushd, popd and dirs; trap DEBUG, CDPATH, the time keyword. Fix: bash -c and bash script.sh run the host bash when no ps-bash launcher is installed beside an embedded module (Linux), and start in the shell directory, not the process directory. v0.14.2: New ExecutableLookup (PsBash.Core): one execvp-style PATH search shared by the interactive shell, test -x, traceroute, tab completion and embedders - directories and files without an execute bit are skipped, so a non-executable file earlier on PATH no longer shadows the real binary (was exit 13 permission denied). find no longer forks stat per entry on Linux/macOS (Owner/Group resolve lazily). 10 more Oils spec cases now pass. v0.14.1: Bash-compatibility batch (about 250 fixes, oracle-verified). New: set -x trace, wait -n, timeout command, local -n namerefs write through, typeset -n/+n, aliases expand at transpile time under expand_aliases, compgen -F/-C/-W/-A, ${v@a/K/k/A}, readonly arrays, terminal tab title follows the running command. Fix: dirs -c/-v/-p, ERR trap LINENO and errtrace. Fix: read (heredoc, -d, -N/-n/-t, REPLY, backslash-newline); parameter expansion (indirect ${!ref}, ${#a[i]}, case-modifying `${v^}`/`${v,,}` with patterns, ${@-w}, negative slices); arrays written in functions reach the caller, per-element operators, unset a[-1]; declare/typeset/readonly/local attributes and declare -p output; `[` / `[[` operand and grouping rules, integer-expression errors; arithmetic edge cases and failing (( )) status; trap signal specs and EXIT traps in subshells; set -e with missing commands (127) and set option handling; alias bodies run as bash, egrep/fgrep; brace and tilde expansion corners; printf 64-bit integers; PIPESTATUS, BASH_VERSINFO, FUNCNAME, LINENO; background jobs see loop variables; rm -rf of the current directory; scripts piped into bash/sh. Release: NuGet publish uses trusted publishing (OIDC). Older versions: https://github.com/standardbeagle/ps-bash/releases'

    } # End of PSData hashtable

